{"campaign_id": "1d55787c-9b86-48a5-ab74-3853d0375648", "completed_at": "2026-10-06T19:45:45Z", "error": null, "id": "M1", "inquiry_id": null, "kind": "measurement", "request": {"description": "Identify the compiled two-link dynamics and quantify how much a one-control-interval bounded motor pulse moves and accelerates each representative IK branch across the official radial range, followed by maximum-command braking.", "measurements": [{"args": ["--output", "campaigns/evaluations/1d55787c-9b86-48a5-ab74-3853d0375648/dynamics_probe.json"], "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/1d55787c-9b86-48a5-ab74-3853d0375648/dynamics_probe.json", "instrument": "python_module", "label": "compiled dynamics and pulse-braking probe", "module": "robot_learning.lab.dynamics_probe"}], "rationale": "The initial model makes dynamic authority versus stabilization the first decision-relevant distinction, but compiled inertias and effective motor authority are unresolved. This measurement separates a low-authority or poorly conditioned reach mechanism from a high-velocity overshoot and braking mechanism before spending the startup allocation on a confounded learned policy. Joint-limit margins and Jacobian singular values also test whether branch and radial geometry must condition the next intervention."}, "result": {"measurements": [{"args": ["--output", "campaigns/evaluations/1d55787c-9b86-48a5-ab74-3853d0375648/dynamics_probe.json"], "instrument": "python_module", "label": "compiled dynamics and pulse-braking probe", "metrics": {"evaluation_artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/1d55787c-9b86-48a5-ab74-3853d0375648/python-module-M1-1-dynamics_probe.json", "evaluation_artifact_contents": {"scope": "structure_only", "sections": [{"entries": 5, "path": "", "type": "object"}, {"path": "/schema_version", "type": "number"}, {"path": "/measurement", "type": "string"}, {"entries": 7, "path": "/model", "type": "object"}, {"path": "/control_interval_s", "type": "number"}, {"entries": 6, "field_names": ["branch", "jacobian_singular_values_m", "joint_limit_margin_deg", "pulse_responses", "qpos_rad", "radius_cm"], "path": "/configurations", "type": "array"}, {"path": "/model/timestep_s", "type": "number"}, {"path": "/model/frame_skip", "type": "number"}, {"entries": 2, "path": "/model/actuator_gear", "type": "array"}, {"entries": 5, "path": "/model/body_mass_kg", "type": "array"}, {"entries": 5, "path": "/model/body_inertia_kg_m2", "type": "array"}, {"entries": 2, "path": "/model/joint_damping", "type": "array"}, {"entries": 2, "path": "/model/joint_armature", "type": "array"}], "truncated": false}, "evaluation_artifact_fingerprint": "ebf85c791a897a550cacd28e2aeca27f0c34ef279776b05cd8f266fb48bf6895"}, "module": "robot_learning.lab.dynamics_probe"}], "paired_comparisons": [], "status": "completed", "tool_provenance": {"campaign_lab_manifest": [{"fingerprint": "af534c4e6e994351ed9b87e4830b9460ccb82b1182319ba160beaf485634f47d", "path": "robot_learning/lab/__init__.py"}, {"fingerprint": "8958de3bead0915f11652e3ec22a1e88e00375e37e354501035f4418aaaa6a8d", "path": "robot_learning/lab/dynamics_probe.py"}], "campaign_lab_publication": {"commit": "b467e15ebb9cc030bb2697e8efebd934388589bd", "fingerprint": "eea289236e44d707ab573a2a5ea294123288f5d04d2fb79b8f685382079bf1fb", "manifest": [{"fingerprint": "af534c4e6e994351ed9b87e4830b9460ccb82b1182319ba160beaf485634f47d", "path": "robot_learning/lab/__init__.py"}, {"fingerprint": "8958de3bead0915f11652e3ec22a1e88e00375e37e354501035f4418aaaa6a8d", "path": "robot_learning/lab/dynamics_probe.py"}]}, "code_parent_commit": "becb96b8d0e09a87aac2a6b0256c34226dbb6c9a", "effective_parameters": {"algorithm": {"name": "ppo"}, "policy": {"activation": "tanh", "net_arch": [64, 64]}, "ppo": {"batch_size": 64, "ent_coef": 0.01, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "gamma": 0.99, "learning_rate": 0.0003, "n_steps": 1024}, "training": {"checkpoint_every_steps": 5000, "n_envs": 1}}, "module_manifest": [{"exists": true, "fingerprint": "8958de3bead0915f11652e3ec22a1e88e0